-- title:
--   Flat classes in H¹(ℚₚ,adρ̄) inject into Honda self-extensions
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field of characteristic an odd prime $p$, let $\mathbb{Z}_p$ act on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ through an algebra structure whose kernel is the ideal generated by $p$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a two-dimensional $k$-space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_k V$ trivial on the fixers of some finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$. Assume (`hunip`) that there is a finite flat cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra $H$ whose reduction $\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}H$ has local Cartier dual, together with a bijection $e$ from the convolution group of $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra maps $H\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ onto $V\times V$ which is additive and carries the action of $\sigma$ in the local Galois group at $p$ by post-composition to $(x_1,x_2)\mapsto(\rho(\sigma)x_1,\rho(\sigma)x_2)$, the action `dualLiftModuleActAd` attached to the zero cocycle. Assume further given: a finite free cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra $H_1$ of rank $|k|^2$ whose reduction has local Cartier dual, an additive and $\rho\circ$`primeLocalToGlobal`-equivariant bijection $e_1$ from the convolution group of $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra maps $H_1\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$ onto $V$; a map $\theta$ from $k$ to bialgebra endomorphisms of $H_1$ with $e_1(f\circ\theta(a))=a\cdot e_1(f)$, multiplicative for composition with $\theta(1)=\mathrm{id}$, and additive for convolution with $\theta(0)$ the convolution unit; a finite-dimensional $k$-space $D$ with $\dim_k D=2$ carrying a Honda system $\mathcal{H}$ for the parameter $0$ (endomorphisms $F,V$ with $F\circ V=V\circ F=0$ and a submodule $L$ satisfying the four Honda axioms); and an additive isomorphism $\iota$ from $D$ onto the Dieudonné module of $\mathbb{Z}/p\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}H_1$ carrying $F$ and $V$ to Frobenius and Verschiebung, $L$ onto the preimage of the Fontaine–Hodge subgroup for `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight`, and the action of $a\in k$ to the Dieudonné functoriality of $\mathrm{id}\otimes\theta(a)$. Then there is an injective map from the set of classes $y$ in $H^1$ of the restriction along `primeLocalToGlobal` of $\operatorname{ad}\bar\rho$ which are the image under `H1π` of some $1$-cocycle $c$ satisfying `ρbar.IsLocallyFlatCocycleAd p c` (a finite flat cocommutative Hopf $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra together with an additive bijection of its $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}_p$-points onto $V\times V$ intertwining the Galois action with the upper-triangular action `dualLiftModuleActAd` of $c$) into $\mathcal{H}$`.selfExt`, the quotient of the module of pairs $(X,Y)$ of $k$-endomorphisms of $D$ with $F\circ Y+X\circ V=0$ and $V\circ X+Y\circ F=0$ by the inner pairs.
--
--   This is the class-separation half of the Fontaine–Conrad comparison between flat cohomology classes at $p$ and self-extensions of a finite Honda system: only injectivity of a map of sets is asserted, with no additivity or $k$-linearity. It is used by [`ResidualGaloisRep.exists_injective_localFlatClassesAd_selfExt_of_hondaSystem_model`](thm.html#ResidualGaloisRep.exists_injective_localFlatClassesAd_selfExt_of_hondaSystem_model) to bound the dimension of the flat local condition in $H^1(\mathbb{Q}_p,\operatorname{ad}\bar\rho)$.
